  "reason": "With no prior evidence, I need to establish a strong baseline while testing the most impactful design axes simultaneously. Config_050 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) combines the strongest prior choices: scgpt (purpose-built single-cell foundation model for RNA), imagenet_vit_l (state-of-the-art vision encoder), transformer aggregation (most expressive for multiprofile), and weighted fusion (learnable combination of modalities). This tests whether the full multimodal pipeline with top-tier encoders and expressive aggregation/fusion can achieve high validation accuracy. If it performs well, it sets a strong bar and I can ablate components in later experiments. If it underperforms, subsequent experiments can isolate which component (encoder choice, aggregation, fusion) is the bottleneck. Given only 10 experiments for 51 configs, starting with the highest-prior configuration maximizes the chance of finding a strong solution early while still providing diagnostic information about the design space."
}

